    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Sales doubled, but AI-chip rout drags AMBQ below every moving average",
               "technical":  "The trend is clearly down. AMBQ closed at $39.68 on 20 Nov 2026, well below all three EMAs (exponential moving averages: smoothed price over 50, 100 and 200 days). EMA50 is $52.32, EMA200 $53.70 and EMA100 $56.03. The fastest average is now the lowest, a bearish order that shows the mid-2026 uptrend has turned down. Momentum is mixed. MACD (a gauge of trend momentum) is -2.85, slightly above its signal line at -3.11. The small positive histogram of +0.26 suggests selling pressure was easing before Friday\u0027s fall, but one more weak session could flip it negative. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 37.39: weak, but not yet oversold. Price sits in the lower part of the Bollinger Bands (a 20-day volatility envelope), about $3.65 above the lower band at $36.03. It is roughly 25% of the way up its 52-week range of $22.12–$91.61, 57% below the high. Volume of 518,600 shares was about 13% above the 20-day average, so the 12.98% drop had some conviction but was not panic-level. Support is at $36.03 and the 5 Nov low near $35.22. Resistance is at the $46.19 middle band, then $52.32.",
               "fundamental":  "The business is doing better than the chart suggests. Q3 2026 results on 10 Nov showed net sales of $38.1M, up 110% year on year and above the company\u0027s own $36–37M guidance. Non-GAAP gross margin reached 48.7%. The GAAP net loss was $7.1M, while the non-GAAP loss was only $1.2M. Seven customers now each buy more than $1M per quarter, up from three a year ago, which reduces reliance on a few buyers. The active customer base grew about 50%. Q4 guidance of $43.5–44.5M points to about $140M in sales for 2026. Cash of $363.5M is more than a third of the roughly $987M market cap. In the AI value chain, Ambiq sits at the far edge: always-on AI running inside wearables. It is building on the SPOT moat with software (heliaAOT) and the Atomiq NPU chip, which is aimed at 2027 production.",
               "news":  [
                            "10 Nov 2026: Q3 beat. Net sales were $38.1M (+110% YoY) against $36–37M guidance. Q4 is guided at $43.5–44.5M with flat gross margin but higher operating costs ($25.5–26.5M), so the guided non-GAAP loss of $(0.09)–$(0.03) per share brackets Q3\u0027s $(0.05).",
                            "11–13 Nov: Several analysts cut price targets, citing lower valuations across the sector rather than weaker results. BofA went to $60 from $75 (Neutral; it wants clearer profitability) and Roth to $75 from $125. Jefferies, Stifel and Northland also trimmed, and most kept positive ratings.",
                            "12–16 Nov: CEO Fumihide Esaka exercised options and sold 109,821 shares (about $5.28M) at $43.92–51.45 under a Rule 10b5-1 plan adopted on 15 May 2026. The sales were scheduled in advance, but they still added shares to the market during the post-earnings bounce.",
                            "20 Nov: AMBQ fell 12.98% during a market-wide AI and chip sell-off in which the Nasdaq 100 lost about 5.6% and Nvidia about 14%. No company-specific news was found for that day.",
                            "Product: Ambiq released heliaPROFILER and heliaAOT 1.0, an AI compiler it says cuts edge inference latency by up to 76%. It was the company\u0027s seventh AI software launch or major release in 2026."
                        ],
               "caution":  "AMBQ is a small-cap (about $987M), thinly traded and very volatile stock. It fell about 49% from late September to 5 Nov and dropped 13% in a single market-wide sell-off. The moving averages are lined up bearishly, and if chip selling continues, the $35–36 area could be tested. The company still loses money on a GAAP basis and Q4 operating costs are rising. CEO selling, past share issuance (the June follow-on at $78) and a still-high valuation leave little room for error if growth slows or a large wearable customer cuts orders.",
               "opportunity":  "The sell-off is coming from falling sector valuations and the broad AI trade, not from a broken business. Revenue doubled, guidance rose, the customer base widened and the non-GAAP loss nearly closed. Cash covers more than a third of market value. For a long-term holder, the gap between the $39.68 price and moving averages around $52–56 mostly reflects sentiment. Early signs of stabilisation would be the $35–36 support holding, RSI turning up and MACD staying above its signal line. Atomiq samples and 2027 production are the next catalysts.",
